---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
    title="tcplot | Claire Nyquist"
    description="tcplot — a meetup group for data visualization enthusiasts exploring creative and scientific plotting."
    image="/images/tcplot(whale).webp"
>
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8">
        <!-- Header -->
        <div class="text-center mb-12">
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl name-gradient mb-6">
                <span class="font-silkscreen font-normal">tcplot</span>
            </h1>
            <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed mb-4">
                <span class="font-silkscreen">tcplot</span> is a Twin Cities community for data visualization
                practitioners, enthusiasts, and storytellers. Whether you are a
                D3 wizard, a Tableau pro, a ggplot2 devotee, or someone who
                appreciates a well-crafted chart, you've found your people.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Colors Image -->
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-12">
            <div class="max-w-2xl w-full rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
                <img
                    src="/images/tcplot(colorswithtext).webp"
                    alt="tcplot data visualization twin cities — colorful mosaic collage of rectangular chart elements"
                    class="w-full h-auto object-contain"
                />
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- About Section -->
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-12">
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
                Our mission is to elevate the data literacy and design standards
                of the MSP area through three core pillars:
            </p>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-600 mb-6">
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">▸</span>
                    <span
                        ><strong class="text-gray-900">Talks:</strong> Hear from local
                        experts and industry leaders on the "why" and "how" of great
                        visualization.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">▸</span>
                    <span
                        ><strong class="text-gray-900">Workshops:</strong> Roll up
                        your sleeves for hands-on sessions where we master new tools,
                        libraries, and design principles.</span
                    >
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
                    <span class="mt-1 text-gray-400">▸</span>
                    <span
                        ><strong class="text-gray-900">Build-a-thons:</strong> Join
                        collaborative coworking where we take datasets and turn them
                        into impactful, interactive, or artistic visual stories.</span
                    >
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Links -->
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-6 mt-12">
            <a
                href="https://tcplot.com"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium"
            >
                tcplot.com
            </a>
            <a
                href="https://www.instagram.com/tcplot/"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium"
            >
                Instagram
            </a>
            <a
                href="https://www.meetup.com/tcplot/?eventOrigin=home_groups_you_organize"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium"
            >
                Meetup
            </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Event: One Dataset, Many Interpretations -->
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-16 mb-12">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">
                Upcoming: One Dataset, Many Interpretations
            </h2>

            <div class="mb-6 text-gray-700">
                <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Saturday, September 26th · 10:00 AM to 12:00 PM CDT
                </p>
                <p class="mt-1">The Coffee Shop NE, 2852 Johnson St NE, Minneapolis, MN</p>
            </div>

            <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 italic">
                One dataset. A room full of ways to see it.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                Nobody sees the dataset until the clock starts. Then everyone gets the same data at the same moment, with total freedom of tools: D3 or ggplot2, Tableau or Excel, Claude Code or colored pencils. Build whatever you see in it, share it in sixty seconds, and discover how differently the room read the same numbers.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                Details at <a href="https://tcplot.com/one-dataset" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">tcplot.com/one-dataset</a>.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Event: Online Feedback Session -->
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-16 mb-12">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">
                Upcoming: tcplot Online Feedback Session
            </h2>

            <div class="mb-6 text-gray-700">
                <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Wednesday, September 30th · 7:00 PM to 8:00 PM CDT
                </p>
                <p class="mt-1">Online, on Google Meet; the link goes out to everyone who RSVPs on Meetup.</p>
            </div>

            <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 italic">
                Bring a chart. Leave with a room full of careful readers on it.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                A structured feedback hour for charts in progress, at any stage and in any tool. Each chart gets a timeboxed crit: the presenter names their audience and one question, readers say what the chart actually communicated before suggesting changes, and the presenter gets the last word. No advance submission; just show up and share your screen.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                Details at <a href="https://tcplot.com/feedback-session" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">tcplot.com/feedback-session</a>.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Event: Mapathon -->
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-16 mb-12">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">
                Upcoming: Mapathon — All About Maps
            </h2>

            <div class="mb-6 text-gray-700">
                <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Saturday, October 24th · 10:00 AM to 12:00 PM CDT
                </p>
                <p class="mt-1">The Coffee Shop NE, 2852 Johnson St NE, Minneapolis, MN</p>
            </div>

            <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 italic">
                Every map is a chart with a place in it.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                A morning devoted entirely to maps, in two acts: bring one map you love (or love to hate) for a two-minute show-and-tell, then we'll build maps of our own and present them. No GIS experience needed.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                Details at <a href="https://tcplot.com/mapathon" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">tcplot.com/mapathon</a>.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Event: Perception Lab -->
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-16 mb-12">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">
                Upcoming: Perception Lab
            </h2>

            <div class="mb-6 text-gray-700">
                <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">
                    Saturday, November 21st · 10:00 AM to 12:00 PM CST
                </p>
                <p class="mt-1">The Coffee Shop NE, 2852 Johnson St NE, Minneapolis, MN</p>
            </div>

            <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 italic">
                The experiments behind every chart, rebuilt live.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                We'll replicate the classic experiments of visual perception as applied to data visualization — rebuild them as tiny web apps, try them for ourselves, and compare what we find with the published results. Coders and non-coders both welcome.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                Details at <a href="https://tcplot.com/perception-lab" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">tcplot.com/perception-lab</a>.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Past Events pointer -->
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-16 mb-12">
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                Curious about past events? Write-ups of everything <span class="font-silkscreen">tcplot</span> has hosted, from data collection in the park to an API build-a-thon, live under Past Events at <a href="https://tcplot.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">tcplot.com</a>.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Petri Image -->
        <div class="flex justify-center mt-12">
            <div class="max-w-2xl w-full rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
                <img
                    src="/images/tcplot(petriwithtext).webp"
                    alt="tcplot data visualization twin cities — collage featuring a scientist with a petri dish, eclipse, and time series chart"
                    class="w-full h-auto object-contain"
                />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
